---
{
  title: "lpml_encode"
}
---
### NAME

    lpml_encode() - Serializes an LPC value into human-readable LPML,
    keeping lines within a column width.

### SYNOPSIS

    varargs string lpml_encode( mixed value, int width );

### DESCRIPTION

    Serializes an LPC value into human-readable LPML, keeping lines within a
    column width.

    Output is meant for files people read and edit: unquoted keys where
    safe, sorted mapping keys, trailing commas, containers expanded only
    when they overflow, and long strings wrapped with LPML string
    concatenation so the decoded value is unchanged.

    Lossy by nature of LPC, not of the format: there are no booleans (1/0
    are written as ints), mapping order is not preserved (keys are sorted),
    and comments in a source file cannot survive a decode/encode round trip.

### PARAMETERS

    value  (mixed)
           The value to serialize.

    width  (int, optional, default: 79)
           Maximum line length. A single string with no safe break point, or
           a very long key, can still exceed it.

### RETURN VALUES

    (string) The LPML text, newline-terminated.

### ERRORS

    If the value contains a non-string mapping key, a circular reference, or
    a type LPML cannot represent (object, function, buffer).

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}write_file("/adm/etc/thing.lpml", lpml_encode(data), 1);{{di0}}
